; TEMPLATE ONLY. Merge with the existing zone; never replace it wholesale.
; 192.0.2.10 is documentation space: replace with the actual static IPv4.
; MX changes redirect ALL incoming @mercav.lat mail. Inventory the old MX first.
mx1                       300 IN A     192.0.2.10
mail                      300 IN A     192.0.2.10
mta-sts                   300 IN A     192.0.2.10
@                         300 IN MX 10 mx1.mercav.lat.
; Publish ONE SPF TXT at @, merging all approved transactional sources.
@                         300 IN TXT   "v=spf1 ip4:192.0.2.10 -all"
; Publish the actual selector/public key generated by Stalwart, not this line:
; mercav202610._domainkey  300 IN TXT   "v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=REPLACE_WITH_PUBLIC_KEY"
_dmarc                    300 IN TXT   "v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:dmarc@mercav.lat; adkim=r; aspf=r"
_mta-sts                  300 IN TXT   "v=STSv1; id=2026101801"
_smtp._tls                300 IN TXT   "v=TLSRPTv1; rua=mailto:tls-reports@mercav.lat"
; Merge CAA with issuers already used by Mercav; don't break existing renewals.
; @                       300 IN CAA 0 issue "letsencrypt.org"
; PTR is configured by the VPS provider: 192.0.2.10 -> mx1.mercav.lat.
; Do not add AAAA until IPv6 routing, firewall, PTR and delivery are verified.
